  <h2>How a bank-transfer redemption works</h2>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li class="good"><b>Verification first.</b> First redemptions require identity and address checks before the operator releases funds.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Account-name match.</b> The receiving account must be in your name; mismatches are a common cause of rejection.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Banking days only.</b> Delivery settles on banking days, so a Friday approval can land the following week.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Caps can apply.</b> McLuck caps redemptions at 10,000 SC per day (4,900 SC in Florida and New York).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Bank transfer vs other rails</h2>
  <p>Bank transfer trades speed for flexibility: <a href="/guides/redemption-methods/crypto/">cryptocurrency</a> settles fastest but needs wallet handling, and <a href="/guides/redemption-methods/gift-card/">gift cards</a> often have lower minimums but are not unrestricted cash. Compare all three in the <a href="/guides/sweepstakes-casino-redemption-methods/">redemption methods guide</a> and the <a href="/research/sweepstakes-casino-redemption-times/">redemption-time research</a>.</p>

